      "text": "To solve the equation \\(7^{x+7} = 8^x\\) and express the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Rewrite the equation using properties of exponents:**\n   \\[\n   7^{x+7} = 8^x\n   \\]\n   We can rewrite \\(7^{x+7}\\) as:\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 7^7 = 8^x\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 2401 = 8^x\n   \\]\n\n2. **Express both sides with the same base:**\n   To combine the terms involving \\(x\\), we take the common base of the exponents, which is \\(2401\\):\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 2401 = 8^x\n   \\]\n   Rewrite \\(2401\\) as \\(7^4\\):\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 7^4 = 8^x\n   \\]\n   Combine the exponents on the left side:\n   \\[\n   7^{x+4} = 8^x\n   \\]\n\n3. **Take the natural logarithm of both sides:**\n   To solve for \\(x\\), we take the natural logarithm (ln) of both sides:\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7^{x+4}) = \\ln(8^x)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Use the logarithm power rule:**\n   Apply the power rule \\(\\ln(a^b) = b \\ln(a)\\):\n   \\[\n   (x+4) \\ln(7) = x \\ln(8)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Distribute and solve for \\(x\\):**\n   Distribute \\(\\ln(7)\\) on the left side:\n   \\[\n   x \\ln(7) + 4 \\ln(7) = x \\ln(8)\n   \\]\n   Move \\(x \\ln(7)\\) to the right side:\n   \\[\n   4 \\ln(7) = x \\ln(8) - x \\ln(7)\n   \\]\n   Factor out \\(x\\) on the right side:\n   \\[\n   4 \\ln(7) = x (\\ln(8) - \\ln(7))\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by \\(\\ln(8) - \\ln(7)\\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{4 \\ln(7)}{\\ln(8) - \\ln(7)}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Express the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\):**\n   We know that \\(\\ln(8) = \\ln(2^3) = 3 \\ln(2)\\) and \\(\\ln(7)\\) remains \\(\\ln(7)\\). Therefore:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{4 \\ln(7)}{3 \\ln(2) - \\ln(7)}\n   \\]\n   Recall that \\(\\ln(2401) = \\ln(7^4) = 4 \\ln(7)\\). So:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{4 \\ln(7)}{4 \\ln(7) - \\ln(7)} = \\frac{4 \\ln(7)}{3 \\ln(7)} = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(x = \\frac{4}{3}\\) and we need it in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{3} = \\log_b 7^7\n   \\]\n   This implies:\n   \\[\n   b = 7^{\\frac{4}{3}}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{7^{\\frac{4}{3}}}\\).",
